---
description: Investigate the requested council claims against actual saved receipts and Native forecast evidence.
args:
  goal: string
  index: RegencyIndex
  opening: RegencySnapshot
  current: RegencySnapshot
returns: RegencyInvestigation
uses: [workOnRegencyBriefing/planRegencyReview, workOnRegencyBriefing/qualifyRegencyClaim, workOnRegencyBriefing/realm/previewRegencySettlement]
---
Determine which observed or projected accounts can answer the actual council question. The planner produces a scope and proposed claims; it does not perform their operations. Acquire only the useful supported Native horizons on this exact current basis and interpret their actual results. Independent readonly forecasts and independent claim judgments may overlap; explicit user ordering or a real data dependency still controls continuation.

Qualify requested factual propositions using the authentic saved accounts or forecasts belonging to the selected revision. A missing horizon is unavailable evidence, not permission to shorten the requested period, borrow a different basis or claim an observation of a projection. Preserve the original requested meaning even when a claim needs a different decomposition. Return actual plan, forecasts and findings for the outer coordinator's next decision; do not commit time or retain an artifact from this investigation.
